# What `pnpm dev` and `pnpm preview` read. Copy this to `.dev.vars` and fill it
# in; that file is gitignored and this one is the list of names.
#
# Every line here is optional. ghdiff with none of them serves every public diff
# and offers no sign-in, which is a working deployment and not a broken one. The
# one exception is SESSION_SECRET: unset means no sign-in, and set to something
# that is not a key throws on the first request rather than sign everybody out
# in silence.

# --- The GitHub App -----------------------------------------------------------
#
# Register a dev App of your own rather than sharing the production one, so a
# laptop never holds the production secret. Its callback URL is
# http://localhost:3000/api/auth/callback — ghdiff derives that from the origin
# the request arrives on, so the App only has to have it registered.
#
# Repository permissions, and no others: Contents read, Pull requests read and
# write, Commit statuses read, Checks read. Turn on "Request user authorization
# (OAuth) during installation" and leave "user-to-server token expiration" on.
# AGENTS.md says why for each.

# From the App's settings page. Looks like Iv23li… — not a secret, but it lives
# here beside the one that is.
GITHUB_APP_CLIENT_ID=

# Generate it on the App's settings page. Signs the code exchange, the refresh,
# and the revocation on sign-out. Never reaches the browser.
GITHUB_APP_CLIENT_SECRET=

# The App's name in a URL, which is what the install link is built from. For an
# App at github.com/apps/ghdiff-dev this is `ghdiff-dev`.
GITHUB_APP_SLUG=

# --- The session cookie -------------------------------------------------------
#
# Seals the httpOnly cookie that holds the reviewer's tokens. 32 or more bytes,
# base64url:
#
#   node -e "console.log(Buffer.from(crypto.getRandomValues(new Uint8Array(32))).toString('base64url'))"
#
# A comma-separated list, newest first. The first key seals every new cookie and
# every key is tried on the way in, so a rotation is two entries for a while and
# costs nobody their session. One key alone would sign out every reviewer.
SESSION_SECRET=

# --- The single-user fallback -------------------------------------------------
#
# A personal access token the server falls back to when a request carries no
# Authorization header and no session cookie. Nothing in the interface asks for
# one; this is here so a deployment for one person can skip the browser step,
# and so curl can authenticate. A viewer resolved from it has no sign-out to
# offer, which is what `fromSession` on `viewer.get` is for.
#
# GITHUB_TOKEN=
